[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3808381204","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115485#issuecomment-3808381204","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115485","id":3808381204,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7i_0kU","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T01:04:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T01:22:27Z","body":"> Force-enabling SSE4.2 causes signal 4 (Illegal instruction) on older processors. By only enabling SSE4.1, similar performance benefits are retained while still maintaining compatibility.\r\n\r\nDid you test this on an actual Core 2 CPU? As far as I know, downgrading to SSE4.1 won't help. We would need to downgrade all the way to SSE2 (which matches Godot 4.4 and prior behavior). See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/discussions/13644.\r\n\r\nThe 32-bit binaries still target SSE2, so they will keep working on Core 2 CPUs for the foreseeable future.\r\n\r\n> Ideally, multiple code paths should be compiled into the same binary. At runtime, the most optimal path can then be selected.\r\n\r\nThis can't be done for autovectorization, only hand-written intrinsics.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3808381204/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3812682989","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115485#issuecomment-3812682989","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115485","id":3812682989,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jQOzt","user":{"login":"xtremeqg","id":15368271,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzY4Mjcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15368271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg","html_url":"https://github.com/xtremeqg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T17:17:27Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T17:44:50Z","body":"> > Force-enabling SSE4.2 causes signal 4 (Illegal instruction) on older processors. By only enabling SSE4.1, similar performance benefits are retained while still maintaining compatibility.\r\n> \r\n> Did you test this on an actual Core 2 CPU? As far as I know, downgrading to SSE4.1 won't help. We would need to downgrade all the way to SSE2 (which matches Godot 4.4 and prior behavior). See also [godotengine/godot-proposals#13644](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/discussions/13644).\r\n\r\nYes, I own a Q9550 (which I used to build and run Godot on), just like the OP of [13644](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/discussions/13644). `/proc/cpuinfo` says it supports `sse4_1`.\r\n\r\nI also own a Q6600, which supports up to SSE3.\r\n\r\n[Intel ARK](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/ark.html) used to have a nice listing of what each core 2 processor supports but a couple years ago they decided to delete all the pages containing core 2 processors.\r\n\r\nThis information can still be [found on Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Intel_Core_2_processors), apparently all core 2 processors on the 45nm node support SSE 4.1","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3812682989/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3812745319","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115485#issuecomment-3812745319","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115485","id":3812745319,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jQeBn","user":{"login":"xtremeqg","id":15368271,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzY4Mjcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15368271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg","html_url":"https://github.com/xtremeqg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T17:27:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T17:27:31Z","body":"> > Ideally, multiple code paths should be compiled into the same binary. At runtime, the most optimal path can then be selected.\r\n> \r\n> This can't be done for autovectorization, only hand-written intrinsics.\r\n\r\nOne could compile the same file multiple times (one for SSE2, one for SSE3, one for SSE4, etc). Extract specific symbols that received performance improvements (a profiler will tell you) using `objcopy`, adding some prefix/suffix in the process. Then, refactor these functions as function pointers which reference the correct function variant after enumerating processor features.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3812745319/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3812832928","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115485#issuecomment-3812832928","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115485","id":3812832928,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jQzag","user":{"login":"xtremeqg","id":15368271,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzY4Mjcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15368271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg","html_url":"https://github.com/xtremeqg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xtremeqg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T17:44:21Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T17:44:21Z","body":"I can probably rewrite the PR to add a build flag, as proposed in [13644](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/discussions/13644).","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3812832928/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3815288855","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115485#issuecomment-3815288855","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115485","id":3815288855,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jaLAX","user":{"login":"asyync1024","id":202911741,"node_id":"U_kgDODBgv_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/202911741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asyync1024","html_url":"https://github.com/asyync1024","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asyync1024/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asyync1024/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asyync1024/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asyync1024/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asyync1024/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asyync1024/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asyync1024/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asyync1024/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asyync1024/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T03:38:14Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T09:48:50Z","body":"> I can probably rewrite the PR to add a build flag, as proposed in [13644](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/discussions/13644).\r\n\r\nI myself would also recommend that, as it would keep the SSE4.2 baseline as default, while enabling custom compilation for older CPUs by users and distros at once. If you can seriously do it, then please do so, it would be a very ideal way of handling baselines.\r\n\r\nFor example the [azahar](https://azahar-emu.org) 3DS emulator has an option to disable the SSE4.2 baseline and allowing custom instruction usage in the CFLAGS etc, means disabling SSE4.2, and still being able to use the highest instruction supported by the non-SSE4.2 CPU.\r\n\r\nThank you for not letting this topic become cold, I was going to bring it up within a few days.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3815288855/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3831292851","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115485#issuecomment-3831292851","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115485","id":3831292851,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kXOOz","user":{"login":"asyync1024","id":202911741,"node_id":"U_kgDODBgv_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/202911741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asyync1024","html_url":"https://github.com/asyync1